      ["Jeg har det bra.","yai hah:r deh: brah:","I'm fine.","The everyday answer to Hvordan går det?"],
      ["Jeg snakker ikke norsk.","yai SNAHK-uhr EEK-uh nohshk","I don't speak Norwegian.","ikke goes after the verb."],
      ["Jeg liker ikke kaffe.","yai LEE:-kuhr EEK-uh KAHF-uh","I don't like coffee.","ikke goes after liker."],
      ["Jeg er glad.","yai ae:r glah:d","I'm glad.","The d in glad is pronounced."],
      ["Jeg er sulten.","yai ae:r SUEL-tuhn","I'm hungry.","Hungry, about a person."],
      ["Jeg er tørst.","yai ae:r toesht","I'm thirsty.","Thirsty, about a person."],
      ["Jeg kan ikke komme.","yai kahn EEK-uh KOHM-uh","I can't come.","ikke sits before the infinitive: kan ikke komme."],
      ["I dag er jeg trøtt.","ee: dah:g ae:r yai troet","Today I'm tired.","Verb second: i dag is one element, then er."],
      ["Jeg er ikke syk.","yai ae:r EEK-uh sew:k","I'm not ill.","ikke goes after er."],
      ["Jeg har det ikke så bra.","yai hah:r deh: EEK-uh soh: brah:","I'm not doing so well.","ikke goes after har: har det ikke."],
      ["Jeg er alltid trøtt.","yai ae:r AHL-tee troet","I'm always tired.","alltid goes after the verb."],
      ["Jeg fryser ikke.","yai FREW:-suhr EEK-uh","I'm not cold.","ikke goes after fryser. Feeling cold is fryser."],
      ["Jeg er sliten.","yai ae:r SLEE:-tuhn","I'm worn out.","Used up by the day. trøtt is sleepy-tired."],
      ["Jeg kjeder meg.","yai HYEH:-duhr mai","I'm bored.","meg matches jeg. A boring person is kjedelig."],
      ["Jeg er opptatt.","yai ae:r OHP-taht","I'm busy.","Busy, or in the middle of something."],
      ["Jeg er lei meg.","yai ae:r lai mai","I'm sad.","lei meg stays together."]
